# No perfect cuboid has two edges in ratio `27 : 364`

Generated by `scripts/cuboid_cert.py` (do not edit by hand):

```
python3 scripts/cuboid_cert.py 14,13,UW
```

These are fibers `(m, n)` of Peschmann's master-tuple parametrization (arXiv:2604.28072),
handled by the generic descent of `LeanPlayground.PerfectCuboid.Descent`. With `U = m² − n²`,
`V = 2mn`, `W = m² + n²`, a perfect cuboid with edges `X = V k`, `Y`, `Z = U k` has
`Y² + U²k²`, `Y² + V²k²` and `Y² + W²k²` all squares, so it gives a solution of `IsSol p q`
for the pair `(p, q, a) = (V, W, U)` and for the pair `(p, q, a) = (U, W, V)`. For each fiber
the certificate lists, for every case of `fiberCases p q a` in order, `.torsion` (a torsion
translate, `torsionOK`) or the modulus `.modulus N l` that rules the case out; the kernel replays
it with `fiberCheckCert`.

* `27 : 364`, the fiber `(m, n) = (14, 13)`. We use the pair `(p, q) = (27, 365)`, `a = 364`; the
  curve `y² = x (x + 729)(x + 133225)` has rank `0` and `Ш[2] = 0`.

The rank computations (PARI/GP) are only the reason to expect the descent to work; the proofs do
not depend on them.

## Main results

* `not_isPerfectCuboid_twentyseven_364` — no perfect cuboid has `27 X = 364 Z`.
